{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792418618,"nonce":"p1RE2qcyd6kmBlj/bbpc7in0I6o=","message":"SCM sidebar and native Ashui graph/panel bridge\n\nCommitted on main: 57f17d7019b0143cc4a4571387127693f4d4a04a.\n\nThe Git extension now declares a Source Control sidebar and Ashui's branch icon (ViewIcons maps it to GIT_BRANCH_LINE). The user supplied VS Code references and requested the graph remain inside the sidebar, with collapsible, resizable Changes and Graph sections. RayScript owns status groups, dense commit rows, reference badges, selection and scene generation. The optional expanded history tab has filters, paging, details and viewport controls.\n\nThe generic bridge adds canvas-kit, ui-button, ui-select and ui-panel-group. Panel groups compose the pinned Ashui Resizable, ResizablePanel, Collapsible, CollapsibleTrigger and CollapsibleContent components; their pointer/keyboard input and animations are native. There is no custom divider input implementation. Native owners are scoped to extension presentation; viewport, panel sizes and open states survive rebuilds. Retained scenes validate commands/regions and decode paths once, while local CanvasKit painting, hover, pan and zoom avoid per-frame script operations. Invalid live drawing properties preserve the last accepted scene and report in the extension Output channel.\n\nThe runtime boundary was clarified with the user: RayScript exceptions fail the affected fiber and need not panic the embedding program. The host process is a separate fault boundary for native faults, not the mechanism for handling script exceptions. The final snapshot test throws from a canvas event handler, observes the error, then verifies another canvas event succeeds in the same host with zero restarts. No Rust runtime changes or Cargo builds were needed.\n\nlibgit2 bindings now expose repositoryStatus, owned paged revwalk cursors, commit metadata/parents and peeled references. The sidebar reads the latest 60 commits; expanded history appends pages of 100. Cursors close explicitly on success, errors and view cleanup. Tests cover child-before-parent order, stable prefix lanes, merge-edge routing, tags, detached and unborn HEAD, cursor lifetime and full/compact graph identities. The pinned C probe checks the author prefix too.\n\nbuild-libgit2.sh generates the ignored git.rayext from the tracked git.rayext.in with the staged library's exact hash. rayde.sh builds/stages it; packaging already invokes the library build. Activation is workspaceContains:.git, onView:scm, and the Git commands; a nested project can activate through its SCM icon or commands. Native approvals remain isolated in snapshot fixtures.\n\nValidation:\n- scripts/rayde.sh --build passed after the panel bridge changes.\n- scripts/check.sh passed with the real compiler and release host.\n- scripts/check-git.sh passed with the checksum-pinned library, real host, deterministic repository fixtures and compact/full graph tests.\n- The full snapshot suite passed during bridge development. After the final panel integration, git plus extension, markdown, views, extensions and debug passed in both schemes using the final compiled harness.\n- Final Git snapshots test the activity icon, grouped status, file opening, refresh, embedded graph selection, real native pointer/keyboard resizing, collapse/keyboard reopen, restored panel sizes, expanded paging/filtering, hover/zoom/pan/fit, malformed-scene containment, owner/cursor cleanup and fiber exception recovery.\n- Dark/light SCM, expanded history, resized and collapsed previews inspected. Docs include copied SCM/history previews.\n- Shell syntax and git diff --check passed.\n\nEvidence: /tmp/git-panels-snapshots.log, /tmp/git-panels-native-final.log, /tmp/git-panels-app-build.log, /tmp/git-graph-checks.log, /tmp/git-graph-all-snapshots.log and /tmp/git-bridge-*-snapshots.log. Previews: bin/snapshots/rayde-{dark,light}-git-scm.png, git-scm-resized.png, git-scm-collapsed.png and git-selected.png. Documentation: docs/git.md and docs/extensions.md.\n\nThe SCM sidebar is currently read only: staging, commit controls, diff tabs, explorer/gutter decorations, status-bar metadata and filesystem watching remain subsequent work. The earlier warm-status performance gate is still not established; this milestone makes no new performance claim. Keep Git and the built-in extension umbrella open.\n\nWork stayed in the canonical main checkout with existing dependency caches. No worktrees, duplicate Cargo targets, sibling repository edits or pushes.","files":null}]}